Section 36 of the Currency and Monetary Order, 2004 is amended by the following new subsection immediately after subsection ( 1) - "(1A) Notwithstanding the generality of subsection (1), on the of this Order -

(a) all assets and liabilities of the Brunei Currency Board by subsection (1) of section 3 of the Currency Act 32) (repealed by this Order) are hereby transferred to and shall vest without further assurance, in the Brunei Currency and Monetary and the Brunei Currency and Monetary Board shall have all necessary to take possession of, recover and deal with such and discharge such liabilities;

(b) all currency notes and coins issued by the Brunei Currency prior to the commencement of this Order shall for all purposes be to have been issued by the Brunei Currency and Monetary

(c) all assets and monies in the Reserve Fund established by

(1) of section 21 of the Currency Act (Chapter 32) (repealed by this Order) are hereby transferred to and shall vest without further in the Reserve Fund established by subsection 11) of section 28 of this Order;

(d) where there are any accounts of the Brunei Currency Board on the commencement of this Order had not been audited by the General under subsection ( 1) of section 26 of the Currency Act 32} jrepealed by this Order), the Auditor General shall forthwith cause such accounts to be audited and to be signed by the Chief Executive Officer and one other member of the Brunei Currency and Monetary Board, and shall thereafter transmit copies of such signed accounts duly certified by him to His Majesty the Sultan and Yang and to the Minister and shall submit to His Majesty the and Yang Di-Pertuan and to the Minister reports on the operation of the Brunei Currency Board for the years to which those accounts respectively relate as if subsection (2) of section 27 of the Currency Act 32) (repealed by this Order) _had not been so repealed;

(e) any permission, consent, approval, authorisation or other decision granted, given or made by the Brunei Currency Board and every deed or other instrument to which the Brunei Curreny Board was or which affected the Brunei Currency Board shall for all purposes, so far as it is not inconsistent with the provisions of this Order and except as otherwise may be expressly provided in this Order or in any other written law, continue and be deemed to have been granted, or made by the Brunei Currency and Monetary Board under the corresponding provisions of this Order; (fJ any proceedings pending on the commencement of this Order shall, so far as they are not inconsistent with the provisions of this Order or of any other written law, continue as if the Brunei Currency and Monetary Board was a party thereto in lieu of the Brunei Currency

(g) where in any other written law reference is made to the Brunei Currency Board, such reference shall mutatis mutandis be read as a reference to the Brunei Currency and Monetary Board.". Made this 2nd. day of Syaaban, 1426 Hijriah corresponding to the 6th. day of September, 2005 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei

HIS MAJESTY THE SULTAN AND YANG Dl-PERTUAN

DARUSSALAM
